From 44db6a4032306a0188d0ce435c9764c7ae37e62e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:13:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 810/810] perf(dsv41): unroll MoE blockscaled K loop across
 stage parity

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-55's series applied through 0809.

Rationale: Under CUDA 13.5 nvcc, keeping ko % stages, (ko // stages) % 2, and
ko < k_full runtime-dependent inside T.serial(k_blocks) stalls pipeline
unrolling and increases register/spill pressure in blockscaled MoE GEMMs.
Unrolling K steps across period = 2 * stages via k_step resolves stage index and
barrier parity at compile time, and passing max_ko elides the tail check and TMA
branch across full-K blocks (0 bytes stack/spills, 191 registers on sm_121a;
w13 E=384 sorted_seq 9.75 ms vs 10.51 ms CUDA 13.0 and 10.78 ms CUDA 13.5, E=128
sorted_seq 9.67 ms vs 10.45 ms CUDA 13.0 and 10.73 ms CUDA 13.5).

Quality implications: None; outputs are bit-identical (max_abs_diff=0) against
both the unpatched kernel and CUDA 13.0 across w13 (E=384, E=128) and w2 (E=384).

Tests: pytest -q -p tblib_stub tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_moe.py
(140 passed in candidate-55-b8 container with moe.py mounted).

Upstream status: local candidate-55 patch
